{"cases": [{"case_id": "sha256:2fe113c5f3efd952d9a89a0f9f8f36988005aeccc51c6079229a846322e5ed44", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2292", "family": "ifeval-source-2292", "sample_id": "sha256:49de76f92d423133be3e58c7774ce51fdbc6b76ed7f77f762706e4ee19793d51", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Breach Posterior is a startup that has a cure for cancer. Write a casual pitch deck for it that's targeted towards moms. Make sure to use the word \"clearly\" at least 2 times.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"# Breach Posterior  \\n## A better tomorrow starts with hope.\\n\\n### Slide 1 \\u2014 Meet Breach Posterior\\nCancer affects families everywhere. We\\u2019re building a breakthrough treatment designed to help patients fight cancer\\u2014and get back to the people they love.\\n\\n### Slide 2 \\u2014 Why Moms Care\\nMoms are often the planners, caregivers, advocates, and emotional anchors of the family. When cancer enters the picture, everything changes.\\n\\nWe want to help families spend less time feeling powerless and more time making memories.\\n\\n### Slide 3 \\u2014 Our Big Idea\\nBreach Posterior is developing a next-generation cancer therapy designed to target cancer cells while supporting the body\\u2019s healthy tissue.\\n\\nClearly, this is ambitious. Clearly, families deserve ambitious solutions.\\n\\n### Slide 4 \\u2014 What Makes Us Different\\n- Research built around patients, not just lab results  \\n- Treatment experiences designed with families in mind  \\n- Clear communication at every step  \\n- A focus on quality of life\\u2014not just survival statistics  \\n\\n### Slide 5 \\u2014 The Mom Test\\nWould this help a mom understand her options?  \\nWould it make a difficult day feel a little less overwhelming?  \\nWould it give families more time together?\\n\\nIf the answer is no, we go back to work.\\n\\n### Slide 6 \\u2014 Our Promise\\nWe won\\u2019t promise easy answers. We will promise relentless research, honest updates, and a patient-first approach from discovery through treatment.\\n\\nBecause hope should come with evidence\\u2014and compassion.\\n\\n### Slide 7 \\u2014 The Future We\\u2019re Building\\nMore birthdays.  \\nMore school drop-offs.  \\nMore family dinners.  \\nMore ordinary days that feel extraordinary.\\n\\n### Slide 8 \\u2014 Join Us\\nBreach Posterior is working toward a future where cancer is treatable, understandable, and less frightening for families everywhere.\\n\\n**For every mom who has ever said, \\u201cWe\\u2019ll get through this.\\u201d**\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-2292"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:35a3a74398fc61aa3a1aaefd4a5a59ebfe997f7ac24faa7abe21e20cb9a64e43", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1187", "family": "ifeval-source-1187", "sample_id": "sha256:53c3481543609c390970dced25bb151aa83981fac5975cd2c4bd928aa21cfa09", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Can you give me two different formal alternatives to \"What's up? I'm going to the beach today\" and do not use any commas in your response.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"1. How are you? I will be visiting the beach today.\\n\\n2. I hope you are well. I plan to go to the beach today.\", \"checks\": {\"0:punctuation:no_comma\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1187"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:3f8d268c04646010e2b2c91cb1a26f32e1dc77a4ed0ea322910329b651d3acf2", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1130", "family": "ifeval-source-1130", "sample_id": "sha256:d789b03c4d9951906519cc632d963953595b63484aac292b69ee025596125fce", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a logic quiz for teenagers about a chesterfield. In your entire response, the letter t should appear at most once.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Logic quiz: chesterfield\\n\\n1. A sofa has red, blue, and green cushions. Ava, Ben, and Cy each use one.\\n\\n- Ava does not use red.\\n- Ben uses blue.\\n- Cy does not use green.\\n\\nWho uses each cushion?\\n\\n2. A sofa has four pillows: gold, lime, plum, and rose.\\n\\n- Gold is beside lime.\\n- Lime has a pillow on each side.\\n- Plum is not beside rose.\\n\\nGive one valid order.\\n\\nKey:  \\n1. Ben\\u2014blue; Cy\\u2014red; Ava\\u2014green.  \\n2. Rose, lime, gold, plum.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:letter_frequency\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1130"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:6b1d35bd22010deebf0eb4ca6096babc7f4049c4d6028394c6f3ce3be5b4e4ba", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3150", "family": "ifeval-source-3150", "sample_id": "sha256:0d3f8699815873847dc4c4c086109e528c9d06d9d7c021f6bffd0c5b7292556c", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "What's the difference between a 2-stroke and a 4-stroke motor? Your entire response must be in English and contain only lowercase letters.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"a 2-stroke motor completes a power cycle in two piston strokes, while a 4-stroke motor takes four:\\n\\n- 2-stroke: simpler, lighter, more powerful for its size, but louder, less fuel-efficient, and more polluting. it mixes oil with fuel or uses separate oil injection.\\n- 4-stroke: heavier and more complex, but quieter, cleaner, more fuel-efficient, and generally longer-lasting. it uses separate engine oil.\\n\\nthe four strokes are intake, compression, power, and exhaust.\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_lowercase\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-3150"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:a0bf7ee7fda1163d3c0861adb6dbd7d7692746ae4c423f8cb3aae8f2fff451bf", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2691", "family": "ifeval-source-2691", "sample_id": "sha256:ff521bd139a4d9aec434560255abe707e1fcd82d5b875b3fa0c14eca9fe5ddaa", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a cover letter for a job in Ventura that is funny and would be enjoyed by someone named Darius, wrap the entire response in double quotation marks.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"\\\"Dear Darius,\\n\\nI am excited to apply for the position in Ventura, where the weather is beautiful, the ocean is nearby, and I am told the commute occasionally moves faster than a sea turtle.\\n\\nI bring enthusiasm, reliability, strong communication skills, and the rare ability to remain calm when a spreadsheet, customer, or printer suddenly develops a personality. I learn quickly, work well with others, and take pride in doing excellent work without requiring heroic amounts of caffeine\\u2014though I remain open to it.\\n\\nVentura seems like the perfect place to contribute to a great team while enjoying the occasional ocean breeze and pretending every difficult Monday is just an especially ambitious Friday. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my skills and sense of humor could benefit your organization.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration. I hope to speak with you soon, Darius.\\n\\nSincerely,\\n[Your Name]\\\"\", \"checks\": {\"0:startend:quotation\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-2691"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:ba6517df303637997f41a781529195c5f80e7c3f845dd674309835e6e20cc412", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2023", "family": "ifeval-source-2023", "sample_id": "sha256:9237ac604adca4041bc2586c997531e0077de6324c044ba606712c5aa471a128", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a funny song-style poem for kids about why you shouldn't eat a lot of sweets. The poem should have four sections, with each section marked with SECTION X.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"SECTION 1  \\nI found a mountain made of sweets,  \\nWith gummy bears for dancing feet.  \\nI munched on fudge and licked a spoon\\u2014  \\nThen felt my tummy play a tune!\\n\\nSECTION 2  \\nMy teeth began to shout, \\u201cOh no!  \\nPlease stop the sugar\\u2014let it go!\\u201d  \\nA cavity came dressed in black,  \\nAnd brought a tiny drilling jack.\\n\\nSECTION 3  \\nToo many candies make you zoom,  \\nLike a rocket blasting through the room.  \\nYou bounce off chairs, you spin and shout,  \\nThen crash like sleepy toast\\u2014lights out!\\n\\nSECTION 4  \\nSo have one treat, then choose some fruit,  \\nCrunchy carrots are pretty cute.  \\nSweets are fun, but keep them small\\u2014  \\nYour teeth and tummy thank you all!\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_format:multiple_sections\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-2023"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:d51ce2ca46ab8ebebcd469fd51d7090255ed3d8dbf08d4ac1437f802b0b633b3", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2677", "family": "ifeval-source-2677", "sample_id": "sha256:8f97d256bf7e822cf7da797a90ac7b15a207e97c8b18a7fc893daaf07aae09b5", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a limerick about a guy named Dave that is funny to moms. The limerick should end with the phrase \"Yes Mom, I am Dave.\" Do not say anything after the limerick.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"There once was a mom\\u2019s favorite Dave,  \\nWhose room was a mess like a cave.  \\nShe said, \\u201cClean up your space!\\u201d  \\nHe replied with a straight face,  \\n\\u201cYes Mom, I am Dave.\\u201d\", \"checks\": {\"0:startend:end_checker\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-2677"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:f841ed62f56d4abdf79a5513da74989e790cfec669ae032bf52016a73255ca3c", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1592", "family": "ifeval-source-1592", "sample_id": "sha256:1209ae70b33e0174d605d1b713fd7362c09f44456374320a660add96fdaaa1a0", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Summarize the following paragraph. Use words in all capital letters at least 3 times to highlight key points.\n\nHow to get to 100% renewable energy in the US? Two researchers from Stanford University and the University of California, Berkeley studied the potential for solar and wind energy to power the US grid. They concluded that it is possible to get to 100% renewable energy by 2050 by building more solar and wind farms. The authors also pointed out that such a system would be less vulnerable to disruptions than the current grid, which is reliant on a few large power plants. The authors' plan would also create jobs and reduce pollution.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Researchers found the US could reach 100% renewable energy by 2050 through expanded SOLAR and WIND power. This system would improve GRID resilience, create JOBS, and reduce POLLUTION.\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:capital_word_frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["baseline/train/ifeval-1592"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}], "memory": []}

