{"cases": [{"case_id": "sha256:39ff734e57451ba8b824011a86012f73e5303d8acb5145312d5a265a5e54c403", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1187", "family": "ifeval-source-1187", "sample_id": "sha256:9010b406160eb4c38e10b949af587cff38d595195cca18b8eba324b1c1642a2b", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:7b4361a5d19b828164a697d72b3a86c2c60a515b0dfbd913ba09e2b1c1eb48db", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Can you give me two different formal alternatives to \"What's up? I'm going to the beach today\" and do not use any commas in your response.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"1. How are you? I will be visiting the beach today.\\n2. I hope you are well. I plan to go to the beach today.\", \"checks\": {\"0:punctuation:no_comma\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1187"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:3e409564fb45296078602ba98964a9a7ec12714da8a64ce57388b29f9d153c14", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2292", "family": "ifeval-source-2292", "sample_id": "sha256:e8f1af11f95147822ec3222f912409e464b4f0e3eee43aaa3881fde3ec1c34c1", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:7b4361a5d19b828164a697d72b3a86c2c60a515b0dfbd913ba09e2b1c1eb48db", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Breach Posterior is a startup that has a cure for cancer. Write a casual pitch deck for it that's targeted towards moms. Make sure to use the word \"clearly\" at least 2 times.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"# Breach Posterior  \\n## A casual pitch for moms who want more tomorrows\\n\\n### Slide 1: The big idea  \\nCancer changes everything in an instant. Breach Posterior is working to change the ending\\u2014with a breakthrough treatment designed to help patients beat cancer and get back to the people they love.\\n\\n### Slide 2: Why moms care  \\nMoms are the planners, comforters, appointment-makers, snack-packers, and family glue. When cancer enters the picture, the whole household feels it.\\n\\nWe\\u2019re building a future where \\u201ccancer diagnosis\\u201d doesn\\u2019t automatically mean \\u201clife on hold.\\u201d\\n\\n### Slide 3: Our solution  \\nBreach Posterior\\u2019s treatment targets cancer at its source while aiming to protect healthy tissue.\\n\\nIn plain English: less guesswork, more precision, and a better path back to everyday life.\\n\\n### Slide 4: Why now  \\nFamilies need treatments that are:\\n\\n- Effective  \\n- Easier to understand  \\n- More accessible  \\n- Designed around real life\\u2014not just the lab  \\n\\nClearly, the science matters. But so does the family dinner, the school pickup, and the bedtime story.\\n\\n### Slide 5: What makes us different  \\nWe combine advanced cancer biology with a patient-first experience:\\n\\n- Clear treatment information  \\n- Support for caregivers  \\n- Practical guidance between appointments  \\n- A team focused on outcomes that families actually feel  \\n\\nBecause clearly, treating the patient means supporting the whole family.\\n\\n### Slide 6: The future we\\u2019re building  \\nA world where more parents are there for graduations, birthdays, messy kitchens, road trips, and ordinary Tuesdays.\\n\\nThat\\u2019s the future Breach Posterior is fighting for.\\n\\n### Slide 7: Our ask  \\nWe\\u2019re looking for partners, investors, clinicians, and advocates who believe families deserve better options.\\n\\nHelp us turn hope into a treatment\\u2014and a treatment into more time together.\\n\\n### Slide 8: Breach Posterior  \\n**More birthdays. More bedtime stories. More tomorrow.**\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2292"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:586e7d5e0a24ba1d2ec8287087a3c0529ca0b5f3de595a5a6e3770f1f5ced44a", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1592", "family": "ifeval-source-1592", "sample_id": "sha256:a01aa51511b3bd6c4e44c3aa1d86cf43945d6ae67a9aff615dfa109b0f740c24", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:7b4361a5d19b828164a697d72b3a86c2c60a515b0dfbd913ba09e2b1c1eb48db", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Summarize the following paragraph. Use words in all capital letters at least 3 times to highlight key points.\n\nHow to get to 100% renewable energy in the US? Two researchers from Stanford University and the University of California, Berkeley studied the potential for solar and wind energy to power the US grid. They concluded that it is possible to get to 100% renewable energy by 2050 by building more solar and wind farms. The authors also pointed out that such a system would be less vulnerable to disruptions than the current grid, which is reliant on a few large power plants. The authors' plan would also create jobs and reduce pollution.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Researchers found the US could reach 100% renewable energy by 2050 through expanded SOLAR and WIND power. This system would be MORE reliable, create JOBS, and reduce POLLUTION.\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:capital_word_frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1592"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:7abe78b4f18259b984efccd4d48ec9a3c345fe7407888ac3130b498efe0fb39c", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-3150", "family": "ifeval-source-3150", "sample_id": "sha256:c2568d85ac61608ea3468ca8009d50edf03466c58e8f16be51a1036396159017", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:7b4361a5d19b828164a697d72b3a86c2c60a515b0dfbd913ba09e2b1c1eb48db", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "What's the difference between a 2-stroke and a 4-stroke motor? Your entire response must be in English and contain only lowercase letters.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"a two stroke motor completes a power cycle in two piston movements and fires once every crankshaft revolution\\n\\na four stroke motor completes a power cycle in four piston movements and fires once every two crankshaft revolutions\\n\\ntwo stroke motors are lighter simpler and more powerful for their size but are usually noisier less fuel efficient and more polluting\\n\\nfour stroke motors are quieter more fuel efficient and cleaner but heavier and more complex\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_lowercase\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-3150"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:87bf281b5d6ce90dd43d07e6924bb730d5c4384ba28122430e878c7136f4dd01", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2677", "family": "ifeval-source-2677", "sample_id": "sha256:fe3ef7cc7dadb8069a3e8a18aacd9b22451294c40f749f995fb90c65a599bf58", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:7b4361a5d19b828164a697d72b3a86c2c60a515b0dfbd913ba09e2b1c1eb48db", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a limerick about a guy named Dave that is funny to moms. The limerick should end with the phrase \"Yes Mom, I am Dave.\" Do not say anything after the limerick.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"There once was a dad named Dave,  \\nWhose socks moms repeatedly saved.  \\nHe\\u2019d ask, \\u201cWhere\\u2019s my phone?\\u201d  \\nWhile holding his own\\u2014  \\n\\u201cYes Mom, I am Dave.\", \"checks\": {\"0:startend:end_checker\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2677"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:8fef3f29cdeec12ef7ca872acab5bfcb7ab45508a58c28d4c7669f938161bec7", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1130", "family": "ifeval-source-1130", "sample_id": "sha256:f2babaec3f4e0736ec574820d3adc3f715d9b0413ef5a48413769634546953dd", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:7b4361a5d19b828164a697d72b3a86c2c60a515b0dfbd913ba09e2b1c1eb48db", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a logic quiz for teenagers about a chesterfield. In your entire response, the letter t should appear at most once.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Logic quiz: chesterfield\\n\\nAva, Ben, and Cia each had one seat: left, mid, or right. Each held one of: cap, mug, or book.\\n\\nClues:\\n1. Ava was mid or right.\\n2. Ben had a mug.\\n3. A book was on mid.\\n4. Cia was right of Ava.\\n5. Cia had a cap.\\n\\nWho had which seat and held what?\\n\\nAnswer: Ava \\u2014 mid, book; Ben \\u2014 left, mug; Cia \\u2014 right, cap.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:letter_frequency\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1130"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:90a2e4316e972041d8925095c7a8132e94f623c99f0d0f0602dbc04f0ae10512", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2023", "family": "ifeval-source-2023", "sample_id": "sha256:eff41b02ef16cae3c5e4fef95f42df3df279d521a8adaaddd3323fbe40034e16", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:7b4361a5d19b828164a697d72b3a86c2c60a515b0dfbd913ba09e2b1c1eb48db", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a funny song-style poem for kids about why you shouldn't eat a lot of sweets. The poem should have four sections, with each section marked with SECTION X.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"SECTION 1  \\nI met a jellybean who wore a tiny hat,  \\nHe said, \\u201cEat ten more!\\u201d\\u2014imagine that!  \\nBut my tummy went rumble, my teeth said, \\u201cPlease!\\u201d  \\n\\u201cToo much sugar makes us sneeze!\\u201d\\n\\nSECTION 2  \\nThe lollipop danced with a chocolate bar,  \\nThey threw a sweet party in my mouth\\u2014how bizarre!  \\nMy teeth wore helmets and shouted, \\u201cWhoa!  \\nWe need some crunchy carrots, bro!\\u201d\\n\\nSECTION 3  \\nCandy can make you zoom like a rocket in flight,  \\nThen leave you droopy by bedtime at night.  \\nYou\\u2019ll bounce off the sofa, then flop like a bean\\u2014  \\nThe sleepiest superhero ever seen!\\n\\nSECTION 4  \\nSo share a few sweets, then munch something wise:  \\nFruit, toast, and veggies in colorful piles.  \\nYour teeth will cheer, and your tummy will sing\\u2014  \\n\\u201cLess candy, more fun!\\u201d\\u2014what a marvelous thing!\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_format:multiple_sections\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2023"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:e3b77e3e247609e6976a12c586dc784bed6812528930fbfd4d69457d83e6cd9c", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2691", "family": "ifeval-source-2691", "sample_id": "sha256:70166324721458100367835e887a32a52cf935ab6266b4b06cee0e412f846cdf", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:7b4361a5d19b828164a697d72b3a86c2c60a515b0dfbd913ba09e2b1c1eb48db", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a cover letter for a job in Ventura that is funny and would be enjoyed by someone named Darius, wrap the entire response in double quotation marks.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"\\\"Dear Darius,\\n\\nI\\u2019m excited to apply for the position in Ventura. I bring strong skills, dependable energy, and the rare ability to make a spreadsheet feel like a team sport. I\\u2019m organized, adaptable, and ready to contribute\\u2014preferably before anyone schedules another \\u201cquick\\u201d meeting that lasts 47 minutes.\\n\\nVentura\\u2019s creativity and coastal spirit are a great match for how I work: thoughtfully, collaboratively, and with enough humor to survive busy days. I\\u2019d love the opportunity to bring my experience, enthusiasm, and excellent snack-selection instincts to your team.\\n\\nThank you for your time and consideration. I\\u2019d welcome the chance to discuss how I can help your organization succeed\\u2014while keeping morale high and coffee levels stable.\\n\\nBest,\\n[Your Name]\\\"\", \"checks\": {\"0:startend:quotation\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/failure/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2691"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}], "memory": []}

