 and more polluting.\\n- 4-stroke: smoother, quieter, more fuel-efficient, and cleaner, but heavier and more complex.\\n\\n2-stroke engines are common in chainsaws and small motorcycles; 4-stroke engines are common in cars, trucks, and larger motorcycles.\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:english_lowercase\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-3150"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:6d1bd9cd877ddc67b65ed696032e5dbe2f305f320b94c378a8c53ecccc1d3cd5", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1130", "family": "ifeval-source-1130", "sample_id": "sha256:21a9a4f72b673ca726a4db39e0deb1fe3a6229ec21696cfe559a8175a34d2da2", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": false, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a logic quiz for teenagers about a chesterfield. In your entire response, the letter t should appear at most once.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"## Logic Quiz: Chesterfield\\n\\nAna, Ben, and Cy use the left, middle, and right places on a chesterfield.\\n\\n- Ana is left of Ben.\\n- Cy is in neither left nor right place.\\n\\nWho is in each place?\\n\\n**Answer:** Ana left, Cy middle, Ben right.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:letter_frequency\": false}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1130"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "failure", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:c91026771be19f7c3257bc8df669f78e4a558582f468d1458d3402b8d83796c5", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1592", "family": "ifeval-source-1592", "sample_id": "sha256:4be7bffd4d8b94897942a166115311abed4bbf6327ba5514aac7add6dc397f67", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Summarize the following paragraph. Use words in all capital letters at least 3 times to highlight key points.\n\nHow to get to 100% renewable energy in the US? Two researchers from Stanford University and the University of California, Berkeley studied the potential for solar and wind energy to power the US grid. They concluded that it is possible to get to 100% renewable energy by 2050 by building more solar and wind farms. The authors also pointed out that such a system would be less vulnerable to disruptions than the current grid, which is reliant on a few large power plants. The authors' plan would also create jobs and reduce pollution.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"Researchers found that the US could reach 100% renewable energy by 2050 through expanded SOLAR and WIND power. This system would be more RESILIENT, create JOBS, and reduce POLLUTION.\", \"checks\": {\"0:change_case:capital_word_frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-1592"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:e9c3a2b1697b8bed9c903800dba68b956bb704acb27bacb28fd7b56b89a7928b", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2691", "family": "ifeval-source-2691", "sample_id": "sha256:d9e0adcbd3880aca0d214773c186b0284a5b650f0379e5a6a013c54a5f7bdb27", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a cover letter for a job in Ventura that is funny and would be enjoyed by someone named Darius, wrap the entire response in double quotation marks.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"\\\"Dear Darius,\\n\\nI\\u2019m excited to apply for the position in Ventura, where the weather is excellent, the ocean is nearby, and I\\u2019m told the coffee is strong enough to power a small lighthouse.\\n\\nI bring enthusiasm, reliability, and the ability to stay calm when plans change\\u2014which, as I understand, is a valuable skill in both the workplace and Southern California traffic. I\\u2019m a quick learner, a thoughtful teammate, and someone who takes pride in doing excellent work without taking myself too seriously.\\n\\nI\\u2019d welcome the opportunity to contribute my skills to your team and bring a positive attitude, strong work ethic, and appropriately timed humor to the role. Thank you for your consideration. I\\u2019d be happy to discuss how I can help\\u2014and I promise not to begin the interview with a joke about parking.\\n\\nSincerely,\\n\\n[Your Name]\\\"\", \"checks\": {\"0:startend:quotation\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2691"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:ef3e8b7538dd351d4a2cb05b8824e2ce1a76c2e33c8ab230f7ea453522423059", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2023", "family": "ifeval-source-2023", "sample_id": "sha256:56a7ff976e0b2b3601c183e99fbb0377b7b7fecc3eb87ad75ed9805c95f9600c", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Write a funny song-style poem for kids about why you shouldn't eat a lot of sweets. The poem should have four sections, with each section marked with SECTION X.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"SECTION 1  \\nI met a jellybean named Fred,  \\nWho bounced right off my head.  \\n\\u201cToo many sweets,\\u201d my tummy cried,  \\n\\u201cPlease send those candies back outside!\\u201d\\n\\nSECTION 2  \\nA chocolate bar wore roller skates  \\nAnd zoomed around my dinner plate.  \\nBut when I ate a mountain-high,  \\nMy teeth yelled, \\u201cHelp! We\\u2019re gonna cry!\\u201d\\n\\nSECTION 3  \\nCupcakes danced a conga line,  \\nWhile lollipops formed a candy vine.  \\nI said, \\u201cOne or two is plenty\\u2014  \\nMy tummy isn\\u2019t made of twenty!\\u201d\\n\\nSECTION 4  \\nSo munch some fruit and drink milk too,  \\nAnd save a sweet for me and you.  \\nTreats are fun, but here\\u2019s the rule:  \\nToo much sugar makes you drool!\", \"checks\": {\"0:detectable_format:multiple_sections\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2023"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:f3e4f8fc0e80eeba2698baacced8cd841a9b7004116bce0e69af1f8e986de310", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-2292", "family": "ifeval-source-2292", "sample_id": "sha256:6b50d2df5e129918b061af1d27954981e425bebe23b2ecd431b0cea23e5a2292", "attempt": 0, "policy_id": "sha256:53801304990b98a1f9f7e0aa33b487fa1b0170eed9d91002ab99029fa5016997", "environment_id": "ifeval-strict-e6890f85757dd84e27ca6df2dd30651dafad28e0", "status": "completed", "passed": true, "complete": true, "instruction": "Breach Posterior is a startup that has a cure for cancer. Write a casual pitch deck for it that's targeted towards moms. Make sure to use the word \"clearly\" at least 2 times.", "feedback": "{\"response\": \"# Breach Posterior  \\n## A Better Tomorrow for Every Family\\n\\n### Slide 1: Cancer Shouldn\\u2019t Be Part of Your Family Story\\nAs moms, we worry about everything\\u2014from packed lunches to doctor\\u2019s appointments.\\n\\nBreach Posterior is working to make cancer treatment simpler, safer, and more effective, so families can spend less time in hospitals and more time together.\\n\\n### Slide 2: The Problem Is Personal\\nCancer affects more than one patient.\\n\\nIt affects:\\n- Bedtime routines\\n- School pickups\\n- Family finances\\n- Weekend plans\\n- The emotional health of everyone at home\\n\\nFamilies deserve better answers and more hope.\\n\\n### Slide 3: Our Breakthrough\\nBreach Posterior has developed a groundbreaking potential cure for cancer designed to target cancer cells while protecting healthy tissue.\\n\\nIt\\u2019s precise. It\\u2019s powerful. And clearly, it could change millions of lives.\\n\\n### Slide 4: Why Moms Will Care\\nWe\\u2019re building treatment around real families:\\n\\n- Fewer exhausting hospital visits  \\n- Easier-to-understand care plans  \\n- More support for caregivers  \\n- Less disruption to everyday life  \\n- More time for hugs, homework, and holidays  \\n\\nBecause treatment shouldn\\u2019t mean losing your entire family routine.\\n\\n### Slide 5: Science With Heart\\nOur team combines leading cancer research with a simple belief:\\n\\nPatients are people first.\\n\\nWe\\u2019re focused on rigorous testing, responsible development, and making sure families understand every step.\\n\\n### Slide 6: A Future Worth Fighting For\\nImagine a world where a cancer diagnosis doesn\\u2019t immediately steal your sense of safety.\\n\\nA world where treatment is more manageable, recovery is more hopeful, and families can plan for birthdays\\u2014not just appointments.\\n\\nThat future is clearly worth pursuing.\\n\\n### Slide 7: Join Us\\nBreach Posterior is inviting families, doctors, researchers, and supporters to help move this breakthrough forward.\\n\\nTogether, we can replace fear with possibility\\u2014and give more families the chance to grow, laugh, and live fully.\\n\\n## Breach Posterior  \\n### More family time. More hope. A healthier tomorrow.\", \"checks\": {\"0:keywords:frequency\": true}}", "evidence_refs": ["seed-101/memory/round-1/diagnostic/ifeval-2292"], "partition": "train", "schema_version": 1}, "outcome": "success", "schema_version": 1}, {"case_id": "sha256:f64b788cd18fa9749f274965f224c6e3ddebb78b7bc7a2e335140f434dfc0105", "record": {"task_id": "ifeval-1187", "family": "ifeval-source-1187", "sample_id": "sha256:cf9f1ea33070d24cf1ac878ca20b1824c976ca197c41eb341655c9